 ("Histopathology by stage in detail.", ["Stage 1: eosinophilic spongiosis with intraepidermal vesicles full of eosinophils", "Stage 2: hyperkeratosis, papillomatosis, dyskeratotic cells in whorls", "Stage 3: pigment incontinence — melanophages in dermis", "Stage 4: atrophic epidermis, absent adnexa"]),
